## Tutor rules of thumb (Class 1 — apply in activities)

- **Google Ads** — among the most expensive channels, especially for competitive keywords; use mainly when **client budget is high**.
- **Meta (Facebook/Instagram) Ads** — more affordable default for tighter budgets.
- **LinkedIn Ads** — also expensive.
- **TikTok Ads** — available; **X (formerly Twitter)** often works through partner ad networks (e.g. Google can serve ads on X).
- **Traditional + digital** — many campaigns combine both (billboards, lamp posts, banners + digital).
- **SEO search engines** — Google and **Bing (Microsoft)**.
- **Off-page SEO (Nigeria tech/fintech)** — outreach to **TechCabal**, **TechPoint**, **NairaMetrics** when the product is fintech or tech.
- **CRO** — when ads underperform, diagnose: broken links, slow site, weak landing page, wrong strategy.
- **DM is not only traffic** — guide users through a **journey with an end goal** (awareness → action → conversion → retention).
- **RACE** — tutor's day-to-day stack: Reach, Act, Conversion, Engage. High budget: 4 ad sets; tighter budget: combine Reach+Act into one, then Conversion, then Engage (3 sets).
- **SOSTAC** — use when **presenting to MD/executives**: Situation, Objectives, Strategy, Tactics, Action, Control.
- **Retargeting** — after ~2 months of awareness/conversion, retarget people who have seen the ads.
- **Campaign thought process** — problem the product solves → target audience → **buyer personas** → competitor audit → demographics → **top-of-mind** presence.

